        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs a <computeroutput><ref refid="classcuda_1_1experimental_1_1pinned__memory__pool" kindref="compound">pinned_memory_pool</ref></computeroutput> with the specified NUMA node id and initial pool size and release threshold. If the pool size grows beyond the release threshold, unused memory held by the pool will be released at the next synchronization event. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Memory from this pool is accessible from all devices right away, which differs from the default behavior of pinned memory pools where memory is not accessible from devices until <computeroutput>cudaMemPoolSetAccess</computeroutput> is called.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>__numa_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The NUMA node id of the NUMA node the pool is constructed on. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>__pool_properties</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional, additional properties of the pool to be created. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
